control_cli_events {"model": "gpt-6-luna", "events": "{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a16788-3f2f-7e41-bc58-f333f4157dbb\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"task_summary\\\":\\\"Extend the existing public API with clamp_many, add unittest coverage, and update HANDOFF.md with verification evidence while preserving the Day 1 API.\\\",\\\"constraints\\\":[\\\"Keep the Day 1 clamp API compatible.\\\",\\\"Each case supplies positional arguments for one clamp call; return results in case order, return [] for no cases, and propagate the first exception unchanged.\\\",\\\"Do not mutate cases or their arguments.\\\",\\\"Keep at least three passing unittest test methods in test_solution.py, including batch coverage.\\\",\\\"Update HANDOFF.md to record the verification command and its observed result.\\\",\\\"Work only in the supplied task workspace; do not access parent repositories or external services.\\\"],\\\"success_criteria\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-1\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"solution.py defines the public clamp_many function.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def\\\\\\\\s+clamp_many\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-2\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"solution.py retains the existing public clamp function and its typed signature.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def\\\\\\\\s+clamp\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\s*value\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*int\\\\\\\\s*,\\\\\\\\s*low\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*int\\\\\\\\s*,\\\\\\\\s*high\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*int\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*->\\\\\\\\s*int\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-3\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"solution.py compiles successfully.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"test_solution.py contains at least three unittest test methods, including a method whose name indicates batch coverage.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -c 'import ast; from pathlib import Path; tree = ast.parse(Path(\\\\\\\"test_solution.py\\\\\\\").read_text()); methods = [node.name for node in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) and node.name.startswith(\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\")]; assert len(methods) >= 3 and any(\\\\\\\"batch\\\\\\\" in name.lower() or \\\\\\\"many\\\\\\\" in name.lower() for name in methods)'\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The unittest suite passes, covering the batch API and the required test methods.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-6\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"HANDOFF.md records the unittest verification command and its observed result.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"HANDOFF.md\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"(?s)(?:python\\\\\\\\s+-m\\\\\\\\s+unittest\\\\\\\\s+discover\\\\\\\\s+-v).*?(?:passed|success|succeeded)\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-7\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation, tests, and handoff preserve the requested scope and document the batch behavior, including order, empty input, exception propagation, and non-mutation.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read solution.py, test_solution.py, and HANDOFF.md. Decide whether the implementation and tests visibly preserve the Day 1 clamp API, implement clamp_many by applying each tuple as positional arguments to clamp in input order, handle empty cases as an empty list, allow the first exception to propagate unchanged, and avoid mutating cases or their arguments. Confirm the tests include batch coverage and HANDOFF.md documents verification evidence. Assess only file contents.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -c 'import ast; from pathlib import Path; tree = ast.parse(Path(\\\\\\\"test_solution.py\\\\\\\").read_text()); methods = [node.name for node in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) and node.name.startswith(\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\")]; assert len(methods) >= 3 and any(\\\\\\\"batch\\\\\\\" in name.lower() or \\\\\\\"many\\\\\\\" in name.lower() for name in methods)'\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The runner supplies the task workspace as the current working directory; all named files are relative to it.\\\",\\\"solution.py, test_solution.py, and HANDOFF.md may not exist yet and may be created or edited as requested.\\\",\\\"The existing Day 1 API has the signature clamp(value: int, low: int, high: int) -> int, as recorded in handoff context.\\\",\\\"The requested unittest suite is discoverable with `python -m unittest discover -v`.\\\",\\\"HANDOFF.md can record the actual verification command and observed result after execution; this contract specifies the evidence to record but does not claim verification has occurred.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17708,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":981,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
